The stats given are for their natural form, which as you observe will
only apply if you have protection from shape changers. However, which
one you're dealing with is still significant: consider for a start the
chances of their being generated, leaving corpses, etc (from
mon2-343.txt):

SPECIES                DIF  FREQ  GRP  ALN  SIZE    WGT   NUTR  GEN  CORPSE%
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ~~~  ~~~~  ~~~  ~~~  ~~~~~~  ~~~~  ~~~~  ~~~  ~~~~~~~
:            chameleon   7    2          0  tiny     100   100  Yes     33
@         doppelganger  11    1          0  medium  1450   400  Yes     33
&            sandestin  15    1#        -5  medium  1500     0  No       0

And different shapeshifters have a preference for taking different
forms. Chameleons have a mild bias towards animal shapes;
doppelgangers have a strong bias towards becoming player-monsters;
sandestins will usually be something from the 'nasties' list.

